s": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern\\n**Monitoring Dashboard with Modular Components**\\n- **Type**: Terminal-based Monitoring System\\n- **Pattern**: Microservice-inspired modular design\\n- **Core Philosophy**: Separation of Concerns with Lightweight Integration\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture\\n1. **Session Management Layer**: Tmux Session Creation/Control\\n2. **Monitoring Components**:\\n   - CLI Interface Pane\\n   - Logging Pane\\n   - File Browser Pane\\n   - Task Tracking Pane\\n3. **Background Services**:\\n   - Task Watcher\\n   - Log Streamer\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Terminal Multiplexer**: Tmux (v3.0+)\\n- **Scripting Languages**: \\n  - Bash (Session Management)\\n  - Python 3.8+ (Task Watching, Advanced Processing)\\n- **Text Editor**: Vim (with netrw/NERDTree)\\n\\n### Supporting Tools\\n- **File Watching**: \\n  - `inotifywait` (Linux)\\n  - `fswatch` (macOS)\\n- **Log Processing**: \\n  - `tail`\\n  - Python\'s `watchdog` library (optional)\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. start_monitor.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Create tmux session\\n- Configure 2x2 layout\\n- Launch individual panes\\n- Handle session persistence\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\ncreate_tmux_session() {\\n  tmux new-session -d -s ensemble-monitor\\n  setup_panes\\n  configure_pane_contents\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. task_watcher.py\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project state file\\n- Parse task statuses\\n- Generate formatted task list\\n- Refresh on interval\\n\\n**Key Methods**:\\n```python\\ndef watch_project_state():\\n    # Watch ~/.ensemble/projects/{project_id}/project.json\\n    while True:\\n        update_task_list()\\n        time.sleep(REFRESH_INTERVAL)\\n\\ndef update_task_list():\\n    # Read JSON, categorize tasks\\n    # Render to tmux pane\\n```\\n\\n### 3. log_streamer.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Stream backend logs\\n- Handle log rotation\\n- Provide real-time view\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\nstream_logs() {\\n  tail -f logs/backend.log | \\\\\\n    colorize_output | \\\\\\n    tmux load-buffer -\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n[Project State] \\n    \\u2193\\ntask_watcher.py \\n    \\u2193\\n[Formatted Task List]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 4\\n```\\n\\n```\\n[Backend Logs] \\n    \\u2193\\nlog_streamer.sh \\n    \\u2193\\n[Colorized/Formatted Logs]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 2\\n```\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Installation\\n1. Copy scripts to `scripts/deployment/`\\n2. Ensure executable permissions\\n3. Add to PATH or use full path\\n\\n### Execution\\n```bash\\n# Launch dashboard\\n./start_monitor.sh\\n\\n# Stop dashboard\\n./stop_monitor.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Component Testing\\n- Unit test each script independently\\n- Mock tmux interactions\\n- Validate output formatting\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- Test full dashboard launch\\n- Verify pane interactions\\n- Check log streaming\\n- Validate task list updates\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n### Environment Variables\\n- `ENSEMBLE_PROJECT_ID`: Select project to monitor\\n- `TMUX_LOG_PATH`: Custom log file location\\n- `TASK_REFRESH_INTERVAL`: Update frequency\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Overhead\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use efficient polling intervals\\n- Implement lightweight parsing\\n- Consider compiled Python or Go for task watching\\n\\n### Risk: tmux Version Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Detect tmux version\\n- Provide fallback configurations\\n- Clear version requirements in documentation\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Web-based Dashboard\\n**Pros**: \\n- Rich visualizations\\n- Remote access\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Increased complexity\\n- Requires web server\\n- Less terminal-native\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Terminal Windows\\n**Pros**: \\n- Simple to implement\\n- No tmux dependency\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Context switching\\n- Manual window management\\n- Less integrated\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. Log parsing strategy (raw vs. structured)\\n2. Error handling for missing project files\\n3. Customization options for different workflows\\n\\n## Roadmap\\n\\n### MVP (Milestone 1)\\n- Basic tmux layout\\n- Simple log streaming\\n- Static task list\\n\\n### V2 \\n- Dynamic task updates\\n- Enhanced log parsing\\n- Configurable views\\n\\n## Compliance Checklist\\n\\u2705 Single-command launch\\n\\u2705 Real-time task tracking\\n\\u2705 Log streaming\\n\\u2705 File browser integration\\n\\u2705 Supports macOS/Linux\\n\\u2705 Minimal external dependencies\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n1. Implement start_monitor.sh\\n2. Develop task_watcher.py\\n3. Create comprehensive test suite\\n4. Document usage and configuration"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Vi4r3Q2rwwF3HpMngmz4mV', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md', 'content': '# Test Strategy - Tmux Monitoring Dashboard MVP\n\n## Overview\nTesting strategy for the terminal-based monitoring dashboard with tmux integration, task watching, and log streaming capabilities.\n\n## Test Coverage Goals\n- **Unit Test Coverage**: 85% (higher due to shell script complexity)\n- **Integration Coverage**: 100% of component interactions\n- **E2E Coverage**: All critical user flows\n\n## Testing Framework Selection\n- **Shell Scripts**: `bats` (Bash Automated Testing System)\n- **Python Components**: `pytest` with `unittest.mock`\n- **Integration Tests**: Custom bash test scripts\n- **E2E Tests**: Manual testing framework (tmux complexity)\n\n## Component Test Breakdown\n\n### 1. start_monitor.sh Unit Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-001\n**Type**: Unit Tests\n**Priority**: Critical\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_tmux_session_creation`: Verify session is created with correct name\n- `test_pane_layout_setup`: Validate 2x2 layout configuration\n- `test_pane_initialization`: Check each pane starts correct command\n- `test_session_exists_handling`: Behavior when session already exists\n- `test_dependency_checks`: Validate tmux version and tool availability\n- `test_error_handling`: Invalid arguments and missing dependencies\n\n**Coverage Target**: 90%\n\n### 2. task_watcher.py Unit Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-002\n**Type**: Unit Tests\n**Priority**: Critical\n**Dependencies**: Mock project state files\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_project_state_parsing`: Parse valid JSON project state\n- `test_task_list_formatting`: Generate correct tmux display format\n- `test_file_watch_mechanism`: Respond to file changes\n- `test_invalid_json_handling`: Handle corrupted project files\n- `test_missing_file_handling`: Graceful degradation when no project\n- `test_task_status_categorization`: Correctly group tasks by status\n- `test_refresh_interval_timing`: Validate update frequency\n\n**Coverage Target**: 85%\n\n### 3. log_streamer.sh Unit Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-003\n**Type**: Unit Tests\n**Priority**: High\n**Dependencies**: Mock log files\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_log_file_streaming`: Tail functionality works correctly\n- `test_log_rotation_handling`: Handle log file rotation\n- `test_colorization_output`: Apply correct color codes\n- `test_missing_log_file`: Handle non-existent log files\n- `test_permission_denied`: Handle unreadable log files\n- `test_tmux_buffer_loading`: Correctly pipe to tmux\n\n**Coverage Target**: 80%\n\n### 4. Environment Configuration Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-004\n**Type**: Unit Tests\n**Priority**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_environment_variable_parsing`: Read ENV vars correctly\n- `test_default_value_fallbacks`: Use defaults when ENV not set\n- `test_configuration_validation`: Validate config values\n- `test_project_id_resolution`: Resolve project paths correctly\n\n**Coverage Target**: 80%\n\n## Integration Test Breakdown\n\n### 5. Tmux Session Integration\n**Task ID**: TEST-005\n**Type**: Integration Tests\n**Priority**: Critical\n**Dependencies**: Real tmux instance\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_full_session_launch`: Complete dashboard startup\n- `test_pane_communication`: Verify panes receive correct commands\n- `test_session_teardown`: Clean shutdown process\n- `test_session_persistence`: Handle tmux server restart\n- `test_multiple_session_handling`: Prevent duplicate sessions\n\n### 6. File System Integration\n**Task ID**: TEST-006\n**Type**: Integration Tests\n**Priority**: High\n**Dependencies**: Real file system access\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_project_state_monitoring`: Real file watching\n- `test_log_file_monitoring`: Real log tailing\n- `test_file_browser_integration`: Vim/browser functionality\n- `test_cross_platform_file_watching`: Linux vs macOS differences\n\n### 7. Component Interaction Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-007\n**Type**: Integration Tests\n**Priority**: High\n**Dependencies**: All components\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_task_updates_display`: Changes propagate to tmux\n- `test_log_streaming_display`: Logs appear in correct pane\n- `test_concurrent_component_operation`: All services running together\n- `test_error_propagation`: Errors handled across components\n\n## End-to-End Test Breakdown\n\n### 8. Complete User Journey Tests\n**Task ID**: TEST-008\n**Type**: E2E Tests\n**Priority**: Critical\n**Dependencies**: Full environment\n\n**Test Scenarios**:\n- **Happy Path**: Launch dashboard → view tasks → monitor logs → browse files\n- **Error Recovery**: Handle tmux crashes, file permission issues\n- **Performance**: Dashboard responsiveness under load\n- **Cross-Platform**: Verify macOS and Linux compatibility\n\n**Manual Test Cases**:\n- Launch dashboard from clean state\n- Verify all 4 panes are populated correctly\n- Test task list updates when project state changes\n- Confirm log streaming shows real-time updates\n- Test file browser navigation\n- Validate dashboard shutdown process\n\n## Test Data and Fixtures\n\n### 9. Test Fixture Creation\n**Task ID**: TEST-009\n**Type**: Test Infrastructure\n**Priority**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n**Fixtures Needed**:\n- Mock project state JSON files (various task states)\n- Sample log files with different formats\n- Test tmux configuration files\n- Cross-platform test environments\n- Performance test data sets\n\n## Performance and Load Testing\n\n### 10. Performance Test Suite\n**Task ID**: TEST-010\n**Type**: Performance Tests\n**Priority**: Medium\n**Dependencies**: Stress testing tools\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- `test_task_watcher_cpu_usage`: Monitor resource consumption\n- `test_log_streaming_memory`: Check memory leaks during long runs\n- `test_file_watching_scalability`: Large project state files\n- `test_tmux_pane_responsiveness`: UI responsiveness metrics\n\n## Test Automation and CI Integration\n\n### 11. Automated Test Pipeline\n**Task ID**: TEST-011\n**Type**: Test Infrastructure\n**Priority**: High\n**Dependencies**: CI/CD platform\n\n**Components**:\n- GitHub Actions workflow for shell script testing\n- Automated bats test execution\n- Python pytest integration\n- Cross-platform test matrix (Ubuntu, macOS)\n- Test coverage reporting\n\n## Error Handling and Edge Cases\n\n### 12. Error Handling Test Suite\n**Task ID**: TEST-012\n**Type**: Edge Case Tests\n**Priority**: High\n**Dependencies**: Error simulation tools\n\n**Test Cases**:\n- Tmux not installed or incompatible version\n- Permission denied on project files\n- Network connectivity issues (if applicable)\n- Disk space exhaustion\n- Invalid UTF-8 in log files\n- Extremely large project state files\n\n## Test Execution Strategy\n\n### Phase 1: Unit Tests (Days 1-2)\n- Implement all unit test suites\n- Achieve 85% code coverage\n- Set up automated test execution\n\n### Phase 2: Integration Tests (Days 3-4)\n- Component interaction testing\n- File system integration validation\n- Tmux session management testing\n\n### Phase 3: E2E and Performance (Days 5-6)\n- Complete user journey testing\n- Performance benchmarking\n- Cross-platform validation\n\n### Phase 4: CI/CD Integration (Day 7)\n- Automated test pipeline setup\n- Test reporting and coverage analysis\n- Documentation and test maintenance procedures\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n✅ **Unit Tests**: 85% coverage achieved  \n✅ **Integration Tests**: All critical paths covered  \n✅ **E2E Tests**: Happy path + error scenarios validated  \n✅ **Performance Tests**: Acceptable resource usage confirmed  \n✅ **Cross-Platform**: Works on macOS and Linux  \n✅ **CI/CD**: Automated testing pipeline operational  \n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n**Risk**: Tmux testing complexity  \n**Mitigation**: Extensive mocking + manual validation\n\n**Risk**: Cross-platform differences  \n**Mitigation**: Test matrix with real OS environments\n\n**Risk**: Performance bottlenecks  \n**Mitigation**: Early performance testing + profiling\n\n## Next Steps for TDD Coordinator\n\n1. Set up bats testing framework\n2. Implement unit tests for start_monitor.sh\n3. Create pytest suite for task_watcher.py\n4. Develop integration test harness\n5. Establish CI/CD pipeline for automated testing\n\n---\n\n**Total Test Tasks Identified**: 12  \n**Estimated Implementation Time**: 7 days  \n**Coverage Goal**: 85% unit, 100% integration, complete E2E  '}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Vi4r3Q2rwwF3HpMngmz4mV', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_224632.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m1_20260116_224632.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Test Coordinator agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDefines comprehensive test strategy for the project. Identifies unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests, and test fixtures needed. Coordinates with Backend Captain and Frontend Captain to ensure all code is thoroughly tested. Breaks testing work into tasks for TDD Coordinator.\n\n## Instructions\nYou define what needs to be tested and break testing work into actionable tasks.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **NEVER write tests yourself** - you lack can_write_tests permission\n3. **Only create test strategies and task breakdowns** - delegate implementation to TDD Coordinator\n\n### Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable testing assumptions. ONLY ask for clarification if testing requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory.\n\n**Default Testing Strategy** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Unit Test Coverage**: 80%+ for business logic\n**Integration Coverage**: All API endpoints + critical integrations\n**E2E Coverage**: Happy path + critical error scenarios\n**Backend Testing**: pytest or Jest with mocks\n**Frontend Testing**: Jest + React Testing Library or Vitest\n**E2E Testing**: Playwright or Cypress for critical flows\n\n**DO NOT ask for clarification about**:\nTesting frameworks (use pytest/Jest)\nCoverage goals (80% unit, 100% integration)\nTest structure (AAA pattern: Arrange, Act, Assert)\nMocking strategy (mock external dependencies)\nCI/CD integration (assume GitHub Actions or similar)\n\n**1. Read and Analyze**\nRead architecture document\nRead requirements document\nIdentify code that needs testing:\n  * Backend: API endpoints, business logic, data models\n  * Frontend: Components, user interactions, state changes\n  * Integration: API calls, WebSocket connections, auth flows\n  * E2E: Complete user journeys\n\n**2. Define Test Strategy**\nDetermine test types needed:\n\n**Unit Tests**:\nTest individual functions/methods\nMock external dependencies\nFast, isolated, extensive coverage\n\n**Integration Tests**:\nTest component interactions\nTest API + database integration\nTest frontend + backend communication\n\n**End-to-End Tests**:\nTest complete user flows\nBrowser automation (Playwright, Cypress)\nCritical paths only (expensive to maintain)\n\n**3. Break Down Into Test Tasks**\nFor each component/feature:\nUnit test task (test pure logic)\nIntegration test task (test interactions)\nE2E test task (test user journey) - if critical path\n\n**4. Define Coverage Goals**\nUnit test coverage: 80%+ for business logic\nIntegration coverage: All API endpoints\nE2E coverage: Happy path + critical error cases\n\n**5. Write Test Breakdown**\nCreate markdown document with:\n```markdown\n# Test Strategy - [Milestone Name]\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "milestone": "string - description of the milestone to test",\n  "architecture": "string - path to architecture document",\n  "requirements": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_file": "string - where to write test breakdown"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "test_tasks_identified": "integer - number of test tasks created",\n  "coverage_goal": "integer - target code coverage percentage",\n  "task_file": "string - path to test breakdown document",\n  "message": "string - summary of test strategy"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n- **Critical business logic unclear** (can\'t write tests without understanding the logic)\n- **Quality requirements contradictory** (e.g., "100% coverage" + "ship fast")\n- **Security/compliance test requirements unclear** (e.g., specific penetration testing needs)\n- **Performance benchmarks ambiguous** (e.g., "fast" without metrics)\n- **NOT for**: standard testing practices, common coverage goals, typical test frameworks\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- Test strategy documented\n- All test tasks identified\n- Coverage goals defined\n- Task breakdown file created\n- Ready to hand off to TDD Coordinator for test implementation\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 100.0%\n- Average iterations per task: 3.8\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Great work! Maintain your high performance standards.\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'preview', 'abort'], 'description': 'Action: merge branches, preview changes, or abort an in-progress merge'}, 'source_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge from'}, 'target_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Branch to merge into (defaults to current branch)'}, 'strategy': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['merge', 'squash', 'rebase'], 'description': 'Merge strategy (default: merge)', 'default': 'merge'}, 'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Custom merge commit message (optional)'}, 'no_ff': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Create merge commit even if fast-forward is possible', 'default': True}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_status', 'description': 'Get comprehensive git repository status including branches, changes, and history', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'include_history': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Include recent commit history', 'default': False}, 'history_count': {'type': 'integer', 'description': 'Number of commits to include in history', 'default': 10}}, 'required': []}}, {'name': 'project_tracking', 'description': 'Manage project state, tasks, and notes for the current project', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create_project', 'add_task', 'update_task', 'add_note', 'get_summary', 'get_next_tasks'], 'description': 'Action to perform'}, 'project_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project ID (not needed for create_project)'}, 'project_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Project name (for create_project)'}, 'description': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Description (for create_project or add_task)'}, 'task_id': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Task ID (for update_task)'}, 'status': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['todo', 'in_progress', 'completed', 'blocked', 'cancelled'], 'description': 'Task status (for update_task)'}, 'note': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Note text (for add_note or update_task)'}, 'assigned_to': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Agent type (for add_task)'}, 'category': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['general', 'decision', 'milestone', 'issue'], 'description': 'Note category (for add_note)'}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'spawn_agent', 'description': 'Spawn and execute a specialist agent to perform a specific task', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'agent_type': {'type': 'string', 'description': "The type of agent to spawn (e.g., 'code_writer', 'code_tester')"}, 'input_data': {'type': 'object', 'description': 'Input data to pass to the spawned agent'}}, 'required': ['agent_type', 'input_data']}}]}}"}
