{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:46:58", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9e27e8ba-5e57-4d0c-bba1-92e17639da1e', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "problem_description": "Develop Tmux Monitoring Dashboard for tracking ensemble agent project tasks",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/monitoring",\n  "test_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/monitoring/tests",\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01R147r6wPfMtemtdgdyg6Hp', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/tmux_monitoring_dashboard/architecture.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01R147r6wPfMtemtdgdyg6Hp', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Tmux Monitoring Dashboard - Architecture Proposal\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Architectural Pattern\\n**Monitoring Dashboard with Modular Components**\\n- **Type**: Terminal-based Monitoring System\\n- **Pattern**: Microservice-inspired modular design\\n- **Core Philosophy**: Separation of Concerns with Lightweight Integration\\n\\n### High-Level Architecture\\n1. **Session Management Layer**: Tmux Session Creation/Control\\n2. **Monitoring Components**:\\n   - CLI Interface Pane\\n   - Logging Pane\\n   - File Browser Pane\\n   - Task Tracking Pane\\n3. **Background Services**:\\n   - Task Watcher\\n   - Log Streamer\\n\\n## Tech Stack\\n\\n### Core Technologies\\n- **Terminal Multiplexer**: Tmux (v3.0+)\\n- **Scripting Languages**: \\n  - Bash (Session Management)\\n  - Python 3.8+ (Task Watching, Advanced Processing)\\n- **Text Editor**: Vim (with netrw/NERDTree)\\n\\n### Supporting Tools\\n- **File Watching**: \\n  - `inotifywait` (Linux)\\n  - `fswatch` (macOS)\\n- **Log Processing**: \\n  - `tail`\\n  - Python\'s `watchdog` library (optional)\\n\\n## System Components\\n\\n### 1. start_monitor.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Create tmux session\\n- Configure 2x2 layout\\n- Launch individual panes\\n- Handle session persistence\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\ncreate_tmux_session() {\\n  tmux new-session -d -s ensemble-monitor\\n  setup_panes\\n  configure_pane_contents\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### 2. task_watcher.py\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Monitor project state file\\n- Parse task statuses\\n- Generate formatted task list\\n- Refresh on interval\\n\\n**Key Methods**:\\n```python\\ndef watch_project_state():\\n    # Watch ~/.ensemble/projects/{project_id}/project.json\\n    while True:\\n        update_task_list()\\n        time.sleep(REFRESH_INTERVAL)\\n\\ndef update_task_list():\\n    # Read JSON, categorize tasks\\n    # Render to tmux pane\\n```\\n\\n### 3. log_streamer.sh\\n**Responsibilities**:\\n- Stream backend logs\\n- Handle log rotation\\n- Provide real-time view\\n\\n**Key Functions**:\\n```bash\\nstream_logs() {\\n  tail -f logs/backend.log | \\\\\\n    colorize_output | \\\\\\n    tmux load-buffer -\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Data Flow\\n\\n```\\n[Project State] \\n    \\u2193\\ntask_watcher.py \\n    \\u2193\\n[Formatted Task List]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 4\\n```\\n\\n```\\n[Backend Logs] \\n    \\u2193\\nlog_streamer.sh \\n    \\u2193\\n[Colorized/Formatted Logs]\\n    \\u2193\\nTmux Pane 2\\n```\\n\\n## Deployment Strategy\\n\\n### Installation\\n1. Copy scripts to `scripts/deployment/`\\n2. Ensure executable permissions\\n3. Add to PATH or use full path\\n\\n### Execution\\n```bash\\n# Launch dashboard\\n./start_monitor.sh\\n\\n# Stop dashboard\\n./stop_monitor.sh\\n```\\n\\n## Testing Strategy\\n\\n### Component Testing\\n- Unit test each script independently\\n- Mock tmux interactions\\n- Validate output formatting\\n\\n### Integration Testing\\n- Test full dashboard launch\\n- Verify pane interactions\\n- Check log streaming\\n- Validate task list updates\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n### Environment Variables\\n- `ENSEMBLE_PROJECT_ID`: Select project to monitor\\n- `TMUX_LOG_PATH`: Custom log file location\\n- `TASK_REFRESH_INTERVAL`: Update frequency\\n\\n## Risks and Mitigations\\n\\n### Risk: Performance Overhead\\n**Mitigation**: \\n- Use efficient polling intervals\\n- Implement lightweight parsing\\n- Consider compiled Python or Go for task watching\\n\\n### Risk: tmux Version Compatibility\\n**Mitigation**:\\n- Detect tmux version\\n- Provide fallback configurations\\n- Clear version requirements in documentation\\n\\n## Alternatives Considered\\n\\n### Alternative 1: Web-based Dashboard\\n**Pros**: \\n- Rich visualizations\\n- Remote access\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Increased complexity\\n- Requires web server\\n- Less terminal-native\\n\\n### Alternative 2: Separate Terminal Windows\\n**Pros**: \\n- Simple to implement\\n- No tmux dependency\\n\\n**Cons**:\\n- Context switching\\n- Manual window management\\n- Less integrated\\n\\n## Open Questions\\n\\n1. Log parsing strategy (raw vs. structured)\\n2. Error handling for missing project files\\n3. Customization options for different workflows\\n\\n## Roadmap\\n\\n### MVP (Milestone 1)\\n- Basic tmux layout\\n- Simple log streaming\\n- Static task list\\n\\n### V2 \\n- Dynamic task updates\\n- Enhanced log parsing\\n- Configurable views\\n\\n## Compliance Checklist\\n\\u2705 Single-command launch\\n\\u2705 Real-time task tracking\\n\\u2705 Log streaming\\n\\u2705 File browser integration\\n\\u2705 Supports macOS/Linux\\n\\u2705 Minimal external dependencies\\n\\n## Recommended Next Steps\\n1. Implement start_monitor.sh\\n2. Develop task_watcher.py\\n3. Create comprehensive test suite\\n4. Document usage and configuration"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01W8E6WrCNk2eqZMhXTxE6AB', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard', 'description': 'Develop a Tmux-based monitoring dashboard for tracking ensemble agent project tasks with modular components and real-time monitoring.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01W8E6WrCNk2eqZMhXTxE6AB', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "1b2b1717", "message": "Created project: Tmux Monitoring Dashboard", "summary": {"project_id": "1b2b1717", "project_name": "Tmux Monitoring Dashboard", "description": "Develop a Tmux-based monitoring dashboard for tracking ensemble agent project tasks with modular components and real-time monitoring.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:46:50.713370", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:46:50.713370", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:46:50.713370", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Tmux Monitoring Dashboard\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01A4uVm2xGCmHjE4xWqz9r5q', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '1b2b1717', 'description': 'Develop start_monitor.sh script for tmux session management', 'assigned_to': 'shell_scripting_expert'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01A4uVm2xGCmHjE4xWqz9r5q', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "4101f70f", "message": "Added task: Develop start_monitor.sh script for tmux session manage