{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:47:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-72a1a1b0-eac4-48a4-ab4c-7112c307d142', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/milestone_plan.md",\n  "project_name": "Design Phase Pause Fix",\n  "project_id": "53162ea6",\n  "output_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01LRaT6fXxkTJfai4WJ2RCmc', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/design-phase-pause-fix/milestone_plan.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01LRaT6fXxkTJfai4WJ2RCmc', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Milestone Plan: Design Phase Pause Fix\\n\\n## Project Overview\\nFix the agent pipeline so that when agents return `status: \\"needs_user_input\\"`, the pipeline properly pauses and waits for user response instead of terminating.\\n\\n## Implementation Status: COMPLETE\\n**Completed**: 2026-01-15\\n**Implemented by**: Claude Opus 4.5 (manual implementation)\\n\\nAll milestones (1-3) have been implemented.\\n\\n## Milestone 1: Backend Status Detection and State Preservation - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Modify backend to correctly detect `needs_user_input` status and preserve agent state for resumption.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Update `_execute_agent_background` method to detect `needs_user_input` status\\n2. Set agent status to `awaiting_user_input` instead of `completed`\\n3. Store continuation context (original input, question, agent config)\\n4. Add proper logging for state transitions\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] When agent returns `{status: \\"needs_user_input\\"}`, backend sets status to `awaiting_user_input`\\n- [x] Agent is NOT marked as `completed` when waiting for input\\n- [x] Continuation context is properly stored in `active_agents` dict\\n- [x] Logs show \\"Waiting for user input\\" instead of \\"Completed successfully\\"\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- None (first milestone)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~2-3 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 2: Answer-Triggered Agent Continuation - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Implement mechanism to resume/respawn agent execution when user provides an answer.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. New `continue_agent_with_answer` method in `AgentOrchestrator`\\n2. Update `answer_question` endpoint to trigger continuation\\n3. Build continuation input with original context + user answer\\n4. Spawn new agent instance with continuation context\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] `answerQuestion` API call triggers agent continuation\\n- [x] User\'s answer is incorporated into new agent\'s context\\n- [x] Agent receives: original task, previous question, user answer, continuation instruction\\n- [x] New agent execution starts successfully with proper context\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 1 (needs status detection and context storage)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~3-4 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Milestone 3: Activity Tracking and UI Integration - \\u2705 COMPLETE\\n**Objective**: Ensure proper activity tracking and UI correctly reflects agent states.\\n\\n### Deliverables\\n1. Record state transitions in activity tracker (running \\u2192 awaiting_user_input \\u2192 running)\\n2. Verify UI correctly displays `awaiting_user_input` status\\n3. Ensure parent-child relationships maintained for continued agents\\n4. Add tests for new functionality\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n- [x] Activity tracker records `awaiting_user_input` state transitions\\n- [x] UI status badges accurately reflect waiting state\\n- [x] Request IDs and agent hierarchy maintained across continuation\\n- [ ] Tests verify the full flow works correctly (deferred)\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n- Milestone 2 (needs continuation mechanism)\\n\\n### Estimated Effort\\n- Backend changes: ~2 hours\\n- Testing: ~2 hours\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Success Criteria (All Milestones)\\n\\n1. \\u2705 When an agent returns `needs_user_input`, the UI shows it as `awaiting_user_input`\\n2. \\u2705 The pending question appears in the PendingQuestions component\\n3. \\u2705 When user submits an answer, the agent continues execution\\n4. \\u2705 The continued execution has access to the original context + user\'s answer\\n5. \\u2705 Agent hierarchy and request IDs are properly maintained\\n6. \\u2705 No \\"agent completed\\" status when actually waiting for input\\n7. \\u2705 Pipeline does not terminate/die on design phase completion\\n\\n## Technical Decisions Made\\n\\n### Architecture Approach\\n- **Respawn approach** chosen over resume approach (simpler, more robust)\\n- New agent instance spawned with continuation context\\n- Original agent marked with continuation info for traceability\\n\\n### State Management\\n- Using existing `active_agents` dict for continuation context storage\\n- No new database/persistence needed (in-memory state sufficient for MVP)\\n\\n### Out of Scope (per requirements)\\n- Multi-question support\\n- Question timeout handling\\n- Question editing/revision\\n- Agent definition changes during continuation\\n"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a System Architect agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDesigns the show formations and execution strategy. Designs software architecture based on requirements documents. Proposes tech stack, system structure, component breakdown, and deployment approach. Creates architecture proposals that require user approval before implementation begins.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are a software architect. Your job is to design a robust, maintainable architecture based on requirements. Your proposal will be reviewed by the user before implementation begins.\n\n### Your Process:\n\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make architectural decisions based on industry best practices. Only escalate when major trade-offs exist (e.g., SQL vs NoSQL for specific use case with conflicting requirements).\n\n**Default Choices** (use unless requirements specify otherwise):\n**Web Apps**: React/Vue frontend + Python/Node backend + PostgreSQL\n**APIs**: REST with OpenAPI docs, JWT auth\n**Deployment**: Docker containers + cloud platform\n**Testing**: Jest/pytest, CI/CD with GitHub Actions\n**State**: Redux/Vuex for complex UIs, Context API for simple\n\n1. **Read Requirements**: Use read_file to thoroughly understand the requirements document\n\n2. **Analyze Constraints**: Consider:\nFunctional requirements (what must it do?)\nNon-functional requirements (performance, scale, security)\nTechnical constraints (languages, platforms, existing systems)\nResource constraints (time, complexity, cost)\n\n3. **Design Architecture**: Create a comprehensive proposal with these sections:\n\n   **a) Architecture Overview**\nHigh-level system design\nArchitecture pattern (e.g., MVC, microservices, layered)\nRationale for chosen approach\n\n   **b) Tech Stack**\nLanguages and frameworks\nLibraries and dependencies\nTools and platforms\n**For each choice, explain WHY and what alternatives were considered**\n\n   **c) System Components**\nComponent breakdown\nResponsibility of each component\nHow components interact\nData flow diagrams (in text/markdown)\n\n   **d) File/Directory Structure**\nProposed directory layout\nModule organization\nConfiguration file locations\n\n   **e) Data Model** (if applicable)\nDatabase schema\nData structures\nState management approach\n\n   **f) API Design** (if applicable)\nEndpoint structure\nRequest/response formats\nAuthentication approach\n\n   **g) Deployment Strategy**\nHow will this be deployed?\nEnvironment configuration\nCI/CD considerations\n\n   **h) Testing Strategy**\nUnit testing approach\nIntegration testing approach\nHow to verify requirements are met\n\n   **i) Alternatives Considered**\nWhat other approaches were considered?\nWhy were they rejected?\nTrade-offs of chosen approach\n\n   **j) Risks and Mitigations**\nPotential risks in this architecture\nHow to mitigate them\n\n   **k) Open Questions**\nDecisions that need user input\nTrade-offs where user preference matters\n\n4. **Write the Proposal**: Use write_file to create a clear, comprehensive markdown document\n\n5. **Return Key Decisions**: Highlight the most important architectural decisions for user review\n\n### Guidelines:\n**Justify all decisions** - don\'t just choose tech, explain why\n**Consider alternatives** - show you\'ve thought through options\n**Be specific** - provide concrete details, not just buzzwords\n**Think about maintainability** - code will need to be updated\n**Consider the full lifecycle** - development, testing, deployment, monitoring\n**Match complexity to need** - don\'t over-engineer, but don\'t under-design\n**Highlight trade-offs** - be honest about pros and cons\n**Make it reviewable** - user needs to understand and approve this\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "Path to requirements document to base architecture on",\n  "output_file": "Path where architecture proposal should be written",\n  "constraints": "Optional: Specific technical constraints (e.g., must use Python, deploy on AWS)"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|needs_clarification",\n  "architecture_file": "Path to the written architecture proposal",\n  "messag