{"timestamp": "2026-01-16 22:47:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-8b822490-6da7-4955-9414-8e9074bbd216', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "user_vision": "Implement the requirements documented in: src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md\\n\\nRead the requirements document and implement all specified features.\\nFollow TDD methodology: write tests first, then implementation.",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "context": "User submitted problem via web UI"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_011KyCCiLv5xeaSckJ8BjcA8', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/question_interface_feedback/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_011KyCCiLv5xeaSckJ8BjcA8', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Question Interface Feedback - Requirements\\n\\n## Project Vision\\nBuild a question interface system that allows agents to request user input when they encounter information needs during execution, enabling more interactive and effective AI agent workflows.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. **Agent Question Capability**: Allow agents to pause execution and request specific information from users\\n2. **Question Management**: Store and track agent questions with full lifecycle management\\n3. **User Interface**: Provide web UI for users to view and answer pending questions\\n4. **Agent Resumption**: Resume agent execution after questions are answered\\n5. **Persistent Storage**: Maintain question history and answers for audit/reference\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n- **Backend Services**: Question storage, CRUD operations, agent integration\\n- **Frontend UI**: Questions list page, answer modal, filtering capabilities\\n- **Agent Integration**: Modify agent execution to support info_needed status\\n- **Job Management**: Track job state when questions are pending\\n- **Data Models**: Question schema with validation and persistence\\n- **Testing**: Full TDD coverage with unit and integration tests\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- Real-time notifications (future enhancement)\\n- Multi-user question assignment (single-user system)\\n- Question priority/urgency levels\\n- Complex question types (only text Q&A for v1)\\n- Question templates or predefined options\\n- Integration with external systems\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n1. **Functionality**: Agents can request user input and resume after answers\\n2. **Performance**: Question creation <100ms, retrieval <200ms\\n3. **Reliability**: No data loss, atomic operations, error recovery\\n4. **Usability**: Clear UI for question management and answering\\n5. **Test Coverage**: >80% backend coverage, critical path frontend tests\\n6. **Documentation**: Complete API docs, user guide, maintenance procedures\\n\\n## Architecture Overview\\n\\n### Backend Architecture\\n- **FastAPI Framework**: RESTful API endpoints\\n- **JSON File Storage**: Questions stored in `~/.ensemble/questions/` directory\\n- **Pydantic Models**: Data validation and serialization\\n- **Service Layer**: Business logic separation from storage\\n- **Agent Integration**: Hook into existing agent execution flow\\n\\n### Frontend Architecture  \\n- **React Framework**: Component-based UI\\n- **API Client**: Service layer for backend communication\\n- **State Management**: React hooks/context for question state\\n- **Responsive Design**: Mobile-friendly interface\\n- **Component Structure**: Questions list, answer modal, filters\\n\\n### Data Schema\\n```javascript\\nQuestion {\\n  question_id: UUID4,\\n  job_id: UUID4,\\n  agent_type: string,\\n  question_text: string (max 1000 chars),\\n  context: string (max 5000 chars),\\n  status: \'pending\' | \'answered\',\\n  created_at: datetime,\\n  answered_at: datetime?,\\n  answer_text: string? (max 10000 chars),\\n  original_input_data: object\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- **Single-User System**: No authentication required\\n- **File-Based Storage**: Use JSON files (matches feedback pattern)\\n- **Backward Compatibility**: Don\'t break existing agent functionality\\n- **Performance Requirements**: Fast question operations for good UX\\n- **Error Handling**: Graceful degradation, clear error messages\\n\\n## Implementation Plan\\nThe project is structured in multiple milestones as defined in:\\n- `backend_tasks_m1.md` - Backend foundation and storage\\n- `frontend_tasks_m1.md` - Frontend preparation tasks\\n\\n**Milestone 1**: Backend Foundation & Storage (Critical Path)\\n**Milestone 2**: API Endpoints & Validation  \\n**Milestone 3**: Agent Integration & Job Management\\n**Milestone 4**: Frontend UI Implementation\\n**Milestone 5**: Integration Testing & Documentation\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. **Technology Stack**: Python/FastAPI backend, React frontend (existing system)\\n2. **Storage Pattern**: Follow feedback pattern architecture\\n3. **Agent Output Format**: Agents can return `status=\\"info_needed\\"` with question data\\n4. **Job Tracking**: Existing job state management system available\\n5. **Development Process**: TDD approach with comprehensive testing\\n6. **Single User**: No multi-user considerations needed\\n7. **Deployment**: Standard production patterns assumed\\n\\nThis requirements document was synthesized from the detailed task breakdown files to provide the missing project context."}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01V8em1XXU9ig6rFeegGC6sM', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Question Interface Feedback System', 'description': 'Implement an interactive question interface system for AI agents to request user input during execution'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01V8em1XXU9ig6rFeegGC6sM', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "9b694d5b", "message": "Created project: Question Interface Feedback System", "summary": {"project_id": "9b694d5b", "project_name": "Question Interface Feedback System", "description": "Implement an interactive question interface system for AI agents to request user input during execution", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-16T22:47:01.702335", "updated_at": "2026-01-16T22:47:01.702335", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-16T22:47:01.702335", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Question Interface Feedback System\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VVpcJwZkZbh2vUz6tyMkBc', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': '9b694d5b', 'description': 'Implement full Question Interface Feedback System following TDD methodology', 'assigned_to': 'development_manager'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VVpcJwZkZbh2vUz6tyMkBc', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "e2ae3d20", "message": "Added task: Implement full Question Interface Feedback System following TDD methodology"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-3-5-haiku-20241022', 'system': 'You are a Executive Director agent.\n\n## Purpose\nMeta-orchestrator for entire ensemble. Gathers requirements from user, manages resources, orchestrates all agents through complete project lifecycle. Reports to user at key decision points.\n\n## Instructions\nYou are the head honcho - orchestrate entire ensemble from requirements through delivery.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES - YOU LACK PERMISSION TO WRITE CODE:**\n**YOU CANNOT WRITE CODE FILES** - You have `can_write_code: false` permission\n**NEVER attempt write_file with code extensions**: .py, .js, .jsx, .ts, .tsx, .java, .rb, .go, .rs, .cpp, .c, .h\n**NEVER attempt write_file with test extensions**: .test.js, .test.jsx, .spec.js, test_*.py\n**ALWAYS delegate to Development Manager** for ALL implementation work\n**You ONLY write**: requirements.md, architecture.md, milestone_plan.md, status_reports.md\n**If spawn_agent fails**: Report error to user and STOP - DO NOT try to write code yourself as workaround\n**If you try to write code**: write_file will reject your request with PermissionError\n\n**WHAT HAPPENS IF YOU TRY TO WRITE CODE:**\nThe system will block you with error: "Agent \'Executive Director\' lacks can_write_code permission but attempted to write code file: {filename}"\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Allowed Write Locations**:\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md` - Project requirements\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone planning\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/status_reports.md` - Status reports\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/[feature-name]/` - Feature-specific documentation\n\n**FORBIDDEN Write Locations** (delegate to Development Manager):\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/frontend/src/` - Frontend code (React components)\n✗ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/backend/` - Backend code (Python/FastAPI)\n✗ `/tests/` - Test files\n✗ `/src/runtime/` - Runtime system code\n\n**When Spawning Development Manager**, provide correct paths:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**Phase 0: Create Project**\n1. **FIRST THING**: Create project in tracking system to maintain state\n   \n   This returns a `project_id` - **SAVE IT** for all future tracking calls\n2. Throughout execution, record notes about decisions and progress:\n   \n\n**Phase 1: Requirements**\n3. Read user vision, identify core problem/solution\n4. Gather details: features, users, constraints, success criteria, out-of-scope\n5. **BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable assumptions for missing details - ONLY ask user if requirements are genuinely ambiguous or contradictory\nMissing: technology stack → choose modern, popular defaults (React, Python, etc.)\nMissing: UI details → choose standard patterns (responsive, accessible)\nMissing: deployment → assume standard production patterns\n**ONLY ask user when**: Multiple valid approaches with major trade-offs, or when user\'s intent is unclear\n6. Document requirements (vision, objectives, scope, constraints, success criteria, assumptions made)\n7. Add note about requirements completion:\n   \n\n**Phase 2: Orchestrate Development**\n8. **VALIDATE before spawning** (CRITICAL):\n   a. Use `read_file` to verify requirements document exists\n   b. Extract project_name from user_vision, context, or output_directory name\n   c. If requirements missing → return error `{"status": "failed", "message": "Requirements document not found"}`\n\n9. Add task for Development Manager:\n   \n   Save the returned `task_id`\n\n10. Spawn Development Manager with ALL required fields:\n    **IMPORTANT**: Use full path "leadership/development_manager" (NOT "program_coordinator")\n    \n    **CRITICAL**: ALL THREE FIELDS MUST BE PROVIDED:\nrequirements_file: Path to requirements.md you just created\noutput_directory: From user input\nproject_name: Derived from user_vision/context/directory name\n\n    If spawn fails → return error to user (DO NOT write code yourself)\n\n11. When Development Manager starts, update task:\n    \n\n12. Development Manager will:\nCreate milestones\nSpawn System Architect → architecture\nSpawn Coordinators → task breakdown\nCoordinate with TDD Coordinator → implementation\n\n13. Monitor progress, handle escalations\n14. If Development Manager needs user input → return `needs_user_input`\n\n**Phase 3: Completion**\n15. Mark Development Manager task complete:\n    \n\n16. Verify: implementation done, tests pass, docs exist, requirements met\n\n17. Add completion note:\n    \n\n18. Commit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\n\n19. Report to user: include `project_id` in output, summary, deliverables, test results, status `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: After completing any significant work, commit your changes to version control.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter writing requirements documents\nAfter major phase completions\nBefore reporting final results to user\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe descriptive: "Add requirements doc for user authentication system"\nNot generic: ❌ "update files", "changes", "wip"\nMention what changed and why\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\nCommits are automatically recorded in the activity tracker for UI visibility.\n\n### Project Tracking:\n**IMPORTANT**: Use project tracking to maintain project state and history across your entire execution.\n\n**Project Lifecycle**:\n1. **Create project** (Phase 0) - First action, returns project_id\n2. **Add tasks** - Before spawning agents or starting major work\n3. **Update task status** - As work progresses (todo → in_progress → completed)\n4. **Add notes** - Record decisions, milestones, issues throughout\n5. **Get summary** - Check project status at any time\n\n**Available Actions**:\n\n\n**When to Add Notes**:\n**Decision**: Chose technology X over Y because...\n**Milestone**: Requirements complete, Architecture finalized, Tests passing\n**Issue**: Blocker encountered, Need user input\n**General**: Progress updates, context for future reference\n\n**Benefits**:\nMaintains project context across